Hi,

please add this board file to ath11k/IPQ5018/hw1.0/board-2.bin.

Hardware: the Ubiquiti UniFi U6 Enterprise, an IPQ5018 access point;
this is the IPQ5018's own 2.4 GHz radio. Its two QCN9074 radios follow
in a separate mail.

Origin: bdwlan.b23 from the vendor firmware for this model
(/lib/firmware/platforms/a654/), unmodified: the vendor device tree
gives this radio qcom,board_id 0x23.

The variant is the qcom,calibration-variant of the board's device tree,
submitted to linux-arm-msm ("arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: add Ubiquiti
UniFi U6 Enterprise").

Board name and md5sum:
  bus=ahb,qmi-chip-id=0,qmi-board-id=255,variant=Ubiquiti-U6-Enterprise
    md5 62c6d13559159771e1e6750e79c08f8b

Tested with WLAN.HK.2.7.0.1-01744-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1 on Linux 7.2:
the radio comes up under ath11k with this board data.

The submission was prepared with an AI coding assistant (Claude Code);
the board files are the vendor's, unmodified, and the testing above
was done on the device.

Andrei

